## Narrative

ChessChallendIII is a fork of Stockfish 19 (`sf_19`, commit `edb0d9db6731067ec50ce619ff372b463bc4dd5d`,
dated 2026-09-05) prepared for the III Chess Challenge. The fork date is the first project
commit (2026-10-26). Phase 1 touches only three upstream files (`src/engine.cpp`, `src/engine.h`,
`src/syzygy/tbprobe.h`) to enforce the competition's five-piece tablebase ceiling (Rule 4);
every touched file carries a dated `Modified by ChessChallendIII` line below its untouched
upstream GPLv3 header, verified by `scripts/check_license.sh`.

The evaluation network is the official Stockfish 19 network, unmodified, CC0-1.0, and is NOT
authored by the team (see PROVENANCE.md). The Rule 2 authorship component lives in
`src/timeman.*` (Phase 4): see `docs/timeman/` and AUTHORSHIP.md when they exist.

Binary sha256 and Project commit come from evidence/01-offline-build.log: the
namespace-severed (`unshare -rn`) fresh-clone build reproduced 2,497,913 nodes
and a byte-identical binary (077d3601…), and the working tree was rebuilt clean
at the same commit to the same hash. The named commit is the HEAD of the last
committed evidence run; later doc-only commits do not change the binary. A
`profile-build` of the same tree produces a different hash with identical
bench nodes; if the shipped binary is a profile-build, record its own hash
and profile here.

